# No trailing slash, deliberately.
#
# `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY called node_modules and nothing else. A
# symlink called node_modules — which is what a linked local dependency is, and
# what several package managers create — is not a directory, so the pattern
# misses it and the link gets committed. That has happened on this codebase once
# already: a symlink pointing at its own parent went into a commit, and every
# checkout afterwards failed with ELOOP.
node_modules

# The build. Nothing serves it — `run.sh` runs Vite — and a checked-in copy is a
# second answer to "what does this page say", which disagrees with the first the
# moment somebody edits `src/`.
dist

# The store this app used to keep beside itself.
#
# Nothing writes here any more: a checklist now lives inside the project it is
# about, in its own folder there — `<project>/.kehikot/checklist/` — see
# `store.ts`. What may still be in this directory is somebody's authored
# material waiting to be moved
# (`bun dev/migrate.ts <project> --apply`) and the `checklists.json.migrated` the
# move leaves behind, which is a backup rather than a store.
#
# Ignored for the reason it always was, which has not changed: it is a person's
# own lists and every tick they filed, and it belongs to the machine the app runs
# on rather than to any repository this directory happens to be sitting in.
data

# Modules on a kehikot host keep this project's data here — checklists, notes,
# journeys, questions — as plain JSON, one folder per module, so it sits beside
# the work instead of inside somebody else's app. It is ignored because it is
# one person's working material and not the project's. Remove these lines to
# share it with everyone who clones this repository.
.kehikot/
